            <div xml:id="d602">

                <pb facs="0816" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg702"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.6363/1248: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-11T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 11,
                                1922—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>169. Your telegram 114, October 12, 4 P.M.<anchor n="50" xml:id="d602-f1"/> and
                    despatch 6520, October 26. If you see no objection you may say to Mr. Pani that
                    your Government has advised you that the draft petroleum bill submitted with
                    your despatch 6450, October 17,<anchor n="51" xml:id="d602-f2"/> is entirely
                    inadequate in the matter of the protection of the lawfully acquired rights of
                    American citizens.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
